      "mergeID": "660f35ee2323467afef9263b",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Standard Lite previously had some bugs with emission not showing up on Android build targets. However, the shader now does not show emission on PC build targets. This applies to both avatars and worlds on PC. It should be mentioned that this issue does not affect old blueprints or content uploaded to the Android build target.\n\nAdditionally, I have provided an image of an avatar using Standard Lite in the editor, and how the same avatar appears in game on a PC client.\n\nOne final note: Standard Lite emission does not preview properly in the editor either. Whenever the scene is reloaded or Play mode is exited, emission will stop previewing on the avatar. This is fixed by clicking on the material in your assets window, but it will once again stop previewing emissions as soon as the scene is reloaded. This behavior has been present ever since Standard Lite was updated with reflections, AO, and detail textures.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1436] Standard Lite emission not working on PC",
      "parentID": "660eb341acd5ef6e6b47d40e",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "657b3706fe6d3382046d7f8f",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}\n\navtr_048dbb42-50d4-4219-8a11-363e0b056e68\n\nPut this together in a fresh project.\n\nThe avatar is supposed to have a red emission all over, which is displayed in the Quest build but not in the PC build.\n\nThe two versions of the avatar haven't been altered between the two builds.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
